WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.152
Greater than ANY means the outer age must be greater than at least one age returned by the inner query.

00:00:06.152 --> 00:00:12.542
For a nonempty set without NULL complications, a helpful intuition is to compare with the minimum.

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:18.152
If your age is greater than the smallest returned age, at least one comparison succeeds.

00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:21.382
Run the query and compare the result with that intuition.

00:00:21.382 --> 00:00:25.987
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:25.987 --> 00:00:30.157
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:30.157 --> 00:00:34.272
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:39.347
In a real setting such as a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists,

00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:44.062
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:46.577
before discussing syntax.

00:00:46.577 --> 00:00:52.000
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
